# Used as virtual_mailbox_maps: a catch-all existence check. Returning a
# match for ANY local-part is deliberate — Postfix only decides whether a
# recipient domain+address is deliverable at all; which specific user or
# capture address it maps to is resolved later, in the Laravel app
# (EmailInboundWebhookController::resolveMailbox), not here. Rejecting
# truly unknown addresses at the app layer (silent 202, no Email record)
# is preferable to rejecting at the SMTP layer, since it avoids leaking
# which addresses are valid to a probing sender.
/^.+@.+\.cubrel\.com$/    1
